- `tests/test_tool_error.py`

`pytest tests/` — 38 passed.
The original stdio orchestrator uppercases every string `id` with `value.upper()` and no format check. `_normalize_id()` follows that rule, so hyphenated and unhyphenated ids are both accepted.

| Input | Sent to the tool |
|---|---|
| `emp-001`, `Emp-001`, `eMp-001`, `EMP-001` | `EMP-001` |
| `emp001`, `Emp001`, `EMP001` | `EMP001` |
| `so-123`, `SO-123` | `SO-123` |
| `so123` | `SO123` |
| `ord-001`, `Ord-001` | `ORD-001` |
| `foo-bar-123` | `FOO-BAR-123` |
| `emp_001` | `EMP_001` |

Other argument keys stay as they are. A non-string `id` is left unchanged.

The README setup section lists these examples. Hub `requirements.md` was left unchanged because this is the existing normalization behavior, not a hyphen-only format.

