`agent/llm_client.py` keeps `get_employee_by_id` and `get_sales_order_by_id` from collapsing into a list call. `_GET_BY_ID_HANDLERS` reads the id out of the question (`emp-001`, `emp001`, `Emp-001`, `so-123`, `so123`, `ord-001`, and “with id …” forms). If the model picks a list tool, drops `id`, or answers in prose, `_apply_get_by_id` still sends that tool with the raw id. `agent/mcp_client.py` uppercases the id before the FastMCP call (`emp-001` → `EMP-001`).

`tests/test_tool_inference.py` covers the cases where the model misses the tool or the id.

No further edits. The working tree is clean; those changes are in the two local commits ahead of `origin/feat/PER-20`.
The AC-2 tool-call test now checks the real FastMCP SSE session, so a mocked `httpx.post` can no longer pass it.

`tests/test_tool_call.py` starts the `mcp` library's FastMCP SSE server and leaves `sse_client` and `httpx` unpatched. A passing call has to:

- open `GET /sse` with `Accept: text/event-stream` and get a `text/event-stream` response
- read the SSE `endpoint` event and POST `initialize`, `notifications/initialized`, and `tools/call` to `/messages/?session_id=...`
- invoke each of the four tools, with `emp-001` and `so-123` sent as `EMP-001` and `SO-123`

A JSON-RPC POST straight to the SSE URL is asserted separately: the server rejects it and no tool runs. `agent/mcp_client.py` already uses `mcp.client.sse.sse_client`, so that file did not change.

The full suite passed: 69 tests.
Historical ID handling is preserved: every string `id` is uppercased, including unhyphenated forms such as `emp001` → `EMP001`.

The original stdio orchestrator (`app/agent/orchestrator.py` in the PER-7 agent) used `value.upper() if key == "id"` with no format check. A hyphen-only pattern would have left `emp001` unchanged. `_normalize_id` already follows that rule, and the docstring now records the source and the formats it covers: hyphenated, unhyphenated, multi-part (`Foo-Bar-123` → `FOO-BAR-123`), and underscore (`emp_001` → `EMP_001`). Separators stay as they are. Non-string `id` values are left unchanged.

